sam: Heads up - noticed per-model configmaps (model-X) updating in k8s but runtime pods aren't picking the new keys after terraform apply. Seen on staging canary, looks like overlay ordering / kustomize generator vs patches is causing stale values. anyone seen this?

maya: yep i noticed on the canary earlier. TF shows configmap resource changed, but controller logs say 'no changes detected' for the mounted files and pods never restarted.

alex: is TF recreating the configmap name or patching data in place? can you paste the relevant resource snippet?

sam: here is the terraform snippet we use in the module (redacted):

```
resource "kubernetes_config_map" "model_conf" {
  metadata {
    name = "model-${var.model_name}-conf"
    annotations = {
      "checksum/config" = md5(file("${path.module}/model.conf"))
    }
    namespace = var.namespace
  }
  data = {
    "model.conf" = file("${path.module}/model.conf")
  }
}
```

sam: TF plan shows the annotation value changed, but kustomize overlay later applies a patch that reorders keys and ends up with the same final checksum in the generated manifest. so deployment annotation that's supposed to trigger rollout doesn't change.

jen: two quick fixes: 1) make Deployment annotate with checksum of the configmap (ensures rollout when cm data changes), or 2) move generator step earlier so kustomize diff sees the new data. i usually do (1) since it's low risk. example: add to deployment spec.template.metadata.annotations: `checksum/config: {{ md5(model.conf) }}`

tim: +1 for deployment annotation. also check if we accidentally use `immutable: true` on those configmaps somewhere - that prevents updates and can cause weird controller behaviour.

maya: raising a tiny PR with the annotation change and a note in the kustomize overlay README. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/1234 (staging only) — i'll run plan/apply then watch the canary.

infra-bot: Pipeline queued for infra/pr-1234: plan -> staging (expected ~4m).

alex: long-term we should standardize the module to surface the checksum as an output and let kustomize generator render it during build, rather than relying on ad-hoc annotation. also add a short test that simulates reordering so we don't regress.

sam: sounds good. action items: sam add deployment annotation in canary patch (in PR), maya apply and monitor, alex file follow-up RFC for module change. will check back after staging run. :thumbsup:
